  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Two long parallel wires <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Q\"></span> are separated by a distance <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"d\"></span>. Each wire carries a current <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"I\"></span>. A magnetic force per unit length <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F\"></span> acts on <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P\"></span> due to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Q\"></span>.</p>\n<p>Now, the distance between the wires is reduced to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{d}{2}\"></span> and the current in <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Q\"></span> is doubled to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2I\"></span>.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>What is the new magnetic force per unit length that acts on <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P\"></span> due to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Q\"></span> after these changes?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2F\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4F\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"8F\"></span></p></li></ol>"
  },
